GROWTH GAPS

1. Episodic Challenge Formats vs. One-Off Tool Drops
Competitors like @dhavalkataria_ achieve over 10,600 average likes and a 19.30% engagement rate by packaging concepts into series (such as "Un-Broke-ing India Episode X"). While @garvit.irl drives massive comment numbers via automated DM funnels, content is currently delivered as isolated resource shares. Creating structured, episodic challenges builds anticipation and increases repeat viewership across the profile.

2. Broad News Hooks and Narrative Tension
Top-performing accounts like @vaibhavsisinty (avg 9775 likes) and @thevarunmayya (avg 25619 likes) hook viewers with mainstream tech narratives (e.g., Sundar Pichai vs. Trump, Bengaluru traffic AI, Tesla Grok). @garvit.irl focuses strictly on deep technical utility (free Claude tokens, GitHub repos). Without narrative-driven hooks at the front of videos, top-of-funnel reach remains capped to niche developer circles.

3. Workflow Stacking vs. Single-Link Aggregation
Creators like @nick_saraev (3631.1 avg likes) frame developer tools as complete stacks (e.g., "5 plugins to install before using Claude Code" or "12 LinkedIn skills"). @garvit.irl shares direct GitHub links, which delivers high utility but lower shareability. Grouping tools into full outcome-based workflows increases video save rates and watch duration.


RECOMMENDED ACTIONS

1. Restrict 100% of Publishing to Reels in the 6:00 PM - 9:00 PM IST Window
Data shows @garvit.irl averages 534 likes on Reels compared to only 35 likes on static posts. Cut static posts entirely for the next 7 days and release 4 to 5 Reels strictly during peak audience activity between 6:00 PM and 9:00 PM IST.

2. Launch a 3-Part "Free AI Architecture" Series
Convert one-off GitHub token tutorials into a serialized case study (e.g., "Building an app using zero dollars and free Claude tokens: Part 1"). Maintain the existing high-performing DM automation comment triggers, but add cliffhangers at the end of each video to drive viewers across multiple Reels.

3. Restructure Hooks with Mainstream Problem Anchors
For the next 3 scripts, avoid opening with generic prompts like "toh bahut log mujhse poochte hain". Instead, mirror high-performing industry hooks by front-loading a provocative claim or direct cost tension (e.g., "Stop paying for Claude subscriptions until you install these two GitHub repos"). Pair the hook with on-screen visual proof in the first 2 seconds to boost initial retention.
